<title>UK: BA load factor falls in September.</title>
<headline>BA load factor falls in September.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said paying passenger traffic in September rose 5.3 percent, with capacity up 7.8 percent to give an overall load factor of 77.6 percent -- down 1.8 percentage points on a year ago.  </p>
<p>Britain's national flag carrier said it had seen a rise of 7.3 percent in its all-important premium business.</p>
<p>British Airways operating statistics Sep 1996 vs Sep 1995</p>
<p>Passengers carried (millions)</p>
<p>UK/Europe - 2.015 vs 1.965 (up 2.6 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 1.029 vs 0.970 (up 6.1 pct)</p>
<p>Total - 3.044 vs 2.935 (up 3.7 pct)  </p>
<p>Traffic (millions Revenue Passenger Kilometres)</p>
<p>UK/Europe - 1,754 vs 1.685 (up 4.1 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 7,436 vs 7.041 (up 5.6 pct)</p>
<p>Total - 9,190 vs 8,726 (up 5.3 pct)</p>
<p>Capacity (millions Available Seat Kilometres)</p>
<p>UK/Europe - 2,360 vs 2,201 (up 7.2 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 9,490 vs 8.793 (up 7.9 pct)</p>
<p>Total - 11,850 vs 10,993 (up 7.8 pct)  </p>
<p>Passenger load factor</p>
<p>UK/Europe - 74.3 percent vs 76.6 percent</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 78.4 percent vs 80.1 percent</p>
<p>Total - 77.6 percent vs 79.4 percent</p>
<p>Cargo - 315 million vs 282 million Cargo Tonne Kilometres</p>
<p>--London newsroom - +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
